  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt[5]{2} & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=1\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=12\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$",
